From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] setup: route parasail's no-SIMD dispatcher fallbacks to
 matching scalar variants

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; the real fix is in jeffdaily/parasail's util/dispatcher.py, which builds the fallback name from the alg alone, plus the regenerated src/*_dispatch.c]

jeffdaily/parasail's generated src/*_dispatch.c pick a SIMD
implementation at run time and, when none is available, fall back to a
scalar one. That fallback is generated as parasail_<alg> (or
parasail_<alg>_scan) for every dispatcher, ignoring its _stats, _table,
_rowcol and _trace qualifiers: e.g. parasail_sw_stats_striped_16 falls
back to plain parasail_sw, which returns a result with no stats, so
result.matches raises "'Result' object has no stats" (test_tables).
The trace variants likewise lose their traceback.

x86 always has at least SSE2 at run time and aarch64/ppc have NEON or
AltiVec, so the fallback is never taken there; riscv64 has no parasail
SIMD backend, so every one of these dispatchers takes it.

Every matching scalar variant exists (parasail_sw_stats,
parasail_sw_stats_table_scan, parasail_sw_trace_scan, ... for sw, nw
and all sg_* flavours), so rewrite each fallback assignment to the one
whose name matches the dispatcher's qualifiers, after the master
archive is unzipped and before configure/make run. Only the fallback
lines (right-hand side without a width suffix) are touched, so SIMD
targets are unaffected.

Checked on riscv64 (qemu-user): all 1092 *_{scan,striped,diag}_{8,16,32,64}
functions exposed by the Python bindings now return a result carrying
the stats/table/rowcol/trace data their name promises, with identical
scores within each alignment algorithm.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 setup.py | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/setup.py b/setup.py
index 32594de..a2c6b40 100644
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -347,6 +347,21 @@ def build_parasail(libname):
     with open(cpuid_c, 'w') as f:
         f.write(cpuid_src)
 
+    # With no SIMD ISA available (riscv64), the generated src/*_dispatch.c
+    # fall back to plain parasail_<alg>[_scan] even for the _stats, _table,
+    # _rowcol and _trace dispatchers, so e.g. sw_stats_striped_16 returns a
+    # result without stats. Point each at its matching scalar variant.
+    fallback_re = re.compile(
+        r'(parasail_(\w+?)_(scan|striped|diag)_\d+_pointer) = parasail_[a-z_]+;')
+    def scalar_fallback(m):
+        base = m.group(2) + ('_scan' if m.group(3) == 'scan' else '')
+        return '{} = parasail_{};'.format(m.group(1), base)
+    for dispatch_c in glob.glob(os.path.join(parasail_root, 'src', '*_dispatch.c')):
+        with open(dispatch_c) as f:
+            dispatch_src = f.read()
+        with open(dispatch_c, 'w') as f:
+            f.write(fallback_re.sub(scalar_fallback, dispatch_src))
+
     root = find_file('configure', parasail_root)
     if root is None:
         print("Unable to find parasail configure script")
